What does `fmt.Println(slices.Collect(Countdown(4)))` print?

```go
func Countdown(n int) iter.Seq[int] {
	return func(yield func(int) bool) {
		for i := n; i > 0; i-- {
			if !yield(i) {
				return
			}
		}
	}
}
```

Using `Countdown` from the previous exercise, what is `total` after this loop?

```go
total := 0
for v := range Countdown(10) {
	if v < 7 {
		break
	}
	total += v
}
```

What does this print?

```go
type Pair[K comparable, V any] struct {
	Key K
	Val V
}

func Swap[A comparable, B any](p Pair[A, B]) (B, A) { return p.Val, p.Key }

func main() {
	v, k := Swap(Pair[string, int]{"x", 1})
	fmt.Println(v, k)
}
```
